<title>USA: Money Store gains after strong Q4.</title>
<headline>Money Store gains after strong Q4.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-02-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Money Store Inc jumped on Wednesday after the consumer and commercial loan company's fourth quarter earnings beat forecasts by Wall Street analysts.</p>
<p>Earlier, Money Store reported fourth quarter fully diluted earnings per share of $0.48, up from $0.34 a year ago. Wall Street's consensus forecast was for $0.41 a share, according to First Call.</p>
<p>Money Store's shares rose 4-1/2 to 25-1/2.  </p>
<p>The Union, N.J.-based company posted a 71 percent rise in net income for the fourth quarter to $29.8 million, compared to $17.5 million a year ago.</p>
<p>The company cited strong loan origination growth in each of its businesses in the fourth quarter.</p>
